-- title:
--   Cumulative killed flow is bounded by the stationary law
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ be a Markov transition matrix on a finite state space $\Omega$, let $A\subseteq\Omega$, and let $\mu$ be a stationary probability distribution for $P$. Put
--
--   $$
--   \lambda(w)=\sum_{z\in A}\mu(z)P(z,w),\qquad F_0(w)=\lambda(w),\qquad F_{s+1}(w)=\sum_{z\notin A}F_s(z)P(z,w).
--   $$
--
--   Thus the flow is killed when it reaches $A$, before taking another transition. For every $t\in\mathbb N$ and $w\in\Omega$,
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{s=0}^{t}F_s(w)\le\mu(w).
--   $$
--
--   This estimate controls the cumulative mass generated by excursions starting from the stationary law restricted to the target.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/CappedReturnSubstationary.lean#L86-L124

